WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.300
A bakery owner wants
a loan for a new oven.

2
00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.580
The bank quotes an interest rate.

3
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.160
That rate is a price,

4
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:08.320
like any other.

5
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.830
It comes from a market for loans.

6
00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:14.210
And the federal government
borrows in that same market.

7
00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:16.260
So when the government borrows more,

8
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.280
can it leave firms with less to invest?

9
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.930
In this mission, you'll
shift a curve in the loanable

10
00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.980
funds market and read off the new rate.

11
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.000
Then you'll look past next year,

12
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.790
to what happens to growth in the long run.

13
00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:35.000
Your mission: figure out what government
borrowing does to the money firms can invest.
